 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No motif on the Prophet ﷺ; a book for «الكتاب والحكمة» only. Coins for «بصدقة», hands for «إصلاح بين الناس»; two paths for «غير سبيل المؤمنين». 115:14-16 «نوله ما تولى» is not glossed (both tafsirs paraphrase it in Allah's first person). The plan title «فضل الله على رسوله» repeated «فضل الله» (113:2-3), so the cover reads «عصمة النبي». STAGING v4: 113 stays ambient: the verse is about the Prophet himself (Allah's favour on him, the group who wanted to mislead him, the Book revealed to him), so nothing may stand for him. 114: a small group of men (3) whispering in a market (private talk, much of it without good); a man speaks on 114:9 (enjoining charity; coins plate) and points to them on 114:12, then walks into the middle on 114:15 (setting things right between people; hands plate ending before the Name). 115: a desert road at dusk; a soft light on 115:7 (the guidance made clear); the man turns his back on 115:10 (following another way than the believers) and leaves on 115:12, the believers go on their way and leave on 115:13, so the stage is empty well before 115:14-20 (the requital and Hell); two-paths plate from 115:11. Nothing is acted on 115:2-3 (no gesture toward an empty side that could stand for the Messenger)."
 },
